        },
        {
          "joint": "jaw-joint",
          "motion": "opening"
        },
        {
          "joint": "jaw-joint",
          "motion": "protraction"
        }
      ],
      "divisionNote": "The tensors are here on Diogo et al. (2008) Table 1, which derives the tensor tympani and tensor veli palatini from the adductor mandibulae A2-PVM bundle and places them on the adductor row for all five mammals it examines — matching the *Ornithorhynchus* and *Rattus* rows on this record. Gest's tables put both on the mylohyoid instead, which is why they stay `membership: \"disputed\"` with the other claimant named.",
